8 3 New Section; Pharmacists and Pharmacies; Ivermectin; Dispensing. Amend RSA 318 by
9 insertingaftersection47-mthefollowingnewsection:
10 318:47-n Ivermectin;Dispensing.
11 I. In this section, "standing order" means a written and signed prescription authored by one
12 or more physicians licensed under RSA 329:12, one or more advanced practice registered nurses
13 licensed under RSA 326-B:18, or one or more physician assistants licensed under RSA 328-D. Such
14 standing order shall allow the pharmacist licensed under RSA 318:18 to dispense Ivermectin under
15 the delegated prescriptive authority of the physician, physician assistant, or advanced practice
16 registered nurse, specify a screening protocol for each patient, specify a requirement to document
17 screening performed and the prescription in the patient's medical record, and include a plan for
18 referring for evaluation and treatment of adverse events; provided that the standing order shall not
19 be used if the patient is pregnant or under 18 years of age. Any such prescription shall be regarded
20 asbeingissuedforalegitimatemedicalpurposeintheusualcourseofprofessionalpractice.
21 II. Licensed pharmacists following standing orders may dispense Ivermectin to persons in
22 this state without a prior prescription. Pharmacies may charge a fee for consultation with the
23 patient.
24 III. A pharmacist, pharmacy, physician, physician assistant, advanced practice registered
25 nurse, or a medical facility that employs a pharmacist, physician, physician assistant, or advanced
26 practice registered nurse, issuing or following standing orders shall be prohibited from seeking
27 personal financial benefit by participating in any incentive-based program or accepting any
28 inducement that influences or encourages therapeutic or product changes or the ordering of tests or
29 services.
30 IV. Apharmacist,physician,advancedpracticeregisterednurse,orphysicianassistantshall
31 beheldtothesamestandardofcareaswhenprescribinganddispensinganyothermedication.
